rs of the 20th century. Two decades after his death, Chavez remains the most significant Latino leader in U.S. history. Yet his life story has been told only in hagiography, until now. In this biography of Chavez, the author offers a searching yet empathetic portrayal. Chavez emerges here as a visionary figure with tragic flaws; a brilliant strategist who sometimes stumbled; and a canny, streetwise organizer whose pragmatism was often at odds with his elusive, soaring dreams. He was an experimental thinker with eclectic passions, an avid, self-educated historian and a disciple of Gandhian non-violent protest. This biography deepens our understanding of one of Chavez's most salient qualities: his profound humanity.","pageCount":548,"publicationYear":2014,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Labor leaders","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-crusades-of-cesar-chavez-a-biography-miriam-pawel"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-crusades-of-cesar-chavez-a-biography-miriam-pawel"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-crusades-of-cesar-chavez-a-biography-miriam-pawel"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Syndicalisme","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-crusades-of-cesar-chavez-a-biography-miriam-pawel"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Droit","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-crusades-of-cesar-chavez-a-biography-miriam-pawel"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Human rights workers","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-crusades-of-cesar-chavez-a-biography-miriam-pawel"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Labor unions","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-crusades-of-cesar-chavez-a-biography-miriam-pawel"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_libra